  (text "TS2068 rear connector (pin names per the TS2068 Technical Manual table 2.4.1-1). Side A on top, confirmed by the v3 bring-up." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 278 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "03a715f9-70e7-437b-8c70-809da5e9c16f"))
  (text "U11/Q1: power-on reset, 1.1 x 220k x 10u = 2.4 s, so the Pico is running before the Z80 starts. C12 is a 25 V ceramic to keep DC-bias loss small." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 282 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a5e42e2d-078e-4329-af32-a01bed42b4fb"))
  (text "SW1 NMI, SW2 TS reset. JP2/JP3: DNP pads for external buttons. JP1 (/BE link) is a solder jumper, closed." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 286 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "505484fe-63e4-4df5-b795-619c4af3c597"))
  (text "R13/R14 only matter out of the 2068 (bench programming): /ROSCS high makes U8 pass the Pico's A14/A15, /IORQ high keeps U6 pointing at the Pico." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 290 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "323dcc41-05dc-410a-992f-a02ee83b1d94"))
